ild through WebGL2; the game does not patch Three.js.\n\n## Content and controls\n\n`levels.js` holds all three authored sectors: solids, breakable bulkheads, hazards, miners, service pads, cave creatures, crystals, start and exit. Coordinates use X/Y as the playable plane and Z for visual depth. Rectangles use center coordinates. `art.js` builds the inked mine and native AnimationMixer clips; `audio.js` synthesizes all music, sounds and formant voices. `network.js` implements ghost races and standalone pairing.\n\nKeyboard: A/D or arrows move, Space/W/up flies, mouse aims and fires (J also fires), E/right click drops a charge, Q scans, Esc/P opens the menu. Gamepad: left stick moves and flies, Cross/A flies, right stick aims, R2/RT or Square/X fires, R1/RB or Circle/B drops a charge, Triangle/Y scans, Options/Menu pauses. Right stick scrolls long menu panels. Touch: invisible left thumb flight stick; right thumb aims and fires; contextual charge button; automatic rescue and aiming assistance.\n\nDev mode is available from Pause. Flight speed, fuel drain, creature speed, blast radius, damage and gravity apply live. Refill, checkpoint return, sector rescue/skip, invulnerability, unlimited power and Rapier collision outlines are included. Gameplay changes mark a shift as training and exclude it from the personal best. Dev tools are disabled in Hub rounds.\n\nThe read-only `window.__game.state` and deterministic `tick()`/input hooks support headless checks. They are the same game systems used during normal play. The complete campaign test uses no teleportation, free fuel, invulnerability or direct rescue calls.\n\n## Multiplayer\n\nAI Hub supports 1–4 players through Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode. Each pilot has an independent cave and sees other pilots in the same sector. The Hub owns timing, transport, progress and results. Its original `session.js`, harness, bridge and round scripts are preserved here.\n\nOutside the Hub, local tabs pair explicitly with BroadcastChannel. Direct two-device pairing uses real WebRTC offer/answer codes. STUN is provided, TURN is not; some restrictive networks require an AI Hub session. Physical gamepads, real touch hardware, real iOS, TV readability on an actual TV, and Internet NAT combinations are unknown; emulation and 1600×900 / 1280×720 screenshots are the available stand-ins.\nEOF\ncat > issue-ledger.json <<'\"'EOF'\n[\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Fourth concurrent software WebGPU copy could fail native pipeline startup\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"critical\\\",\\\"foundBy\\\":\\\"four-player official Hub harness\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":true},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Disposing a failed renderer left callbacks attached to stale resource caches\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"critical\\\",\\\"foundBy\\\":\\\"recovery regression in four-player Hub harness\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":true},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Pilot collision could kick a charge beyond the wall blast range\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"foundBy\\\":\\\"physical-input campaign AI playthrough\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":true},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Steam vent art did not distinguish the safe and dangerous cycle\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"foundBy\\\":\\\"visual and hazard review\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":true},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Browser pan gestures cancelled touch flight pointers\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"critical\\\",\\\"foundBy\\\":\\\"native multitouch CDP input test\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":true},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Landing underwater could recharge power faster than water drained it\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"foundBy\\\":\\\"flood hazard test review\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":true},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Title mission notes overlapped the pilot portrait\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"foundBy\\\":\\\"title screenshot review\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":true},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Controller had no way to scroll the long credits panel\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"foundBy\\\":\\\"controller requirements audit and scrolling test\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":true},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Escape could not return from title-origin submenus\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"foundBy\\\":\\\"keyboard requirements audit and navigation test\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":true},\n {\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Race results kept waiting after a rival disconnected\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"foundBy\\\":\\\"standalone results audit and disconnect test\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":true}\n]\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='metadata.json';d=json.load(open(p))\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless Chromium 153 with native WebGPU and WebGL2 visual checks; scripted full-campaign playthrough without cheats; standard gamepad emulation; native multitouch emulation; offline/live Web Audio; actual BroadcastChannel and WebRTC; official Hub 2-player, adverse 4-player and host-leave scenarios. Real hardware input feel and Internet NAT reachability: unknown.'\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n '10 issues were caught across automated checks, visual review and controller audit; all were fixed. The development issue ledger records each one.',\n '3 were game breaking during development: fourth-copy native GPU startup, stale GPU recovery callbacks, and browser gestures cancelling touch flight. All are fixed.',\n 'The complete three-sector physical-input AI playthrough without cheats: it uses the flight, laser and timed-charge systems, opens every bulkhead, rescues all six miners and reaches victory.',\n 'Native headless WebGPU screenshots were blank despite valid game state. The same scenes were checked visually through the WebGPURenderer WebGL2 backend instead.'\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n 'Three.js native AnimationMixer clips and cel-shaded node materials make procedural characters and caves feel cohesive.',\n 'Four concurrent software WebGPU copies exposed native pipeline errors; renderer disposal then exposed stale cache callbacks. Recovery now retires the failed device and rebuilds a fresh scene through WebGL2.',\n 'The data-driven rescue campaign, jetpack controls, destructible walls, controller UI and ghost-race lifecycle.',\n 'Recovering cleanly from asynchronous GPU initialization failure while keeping physics and game state valid.',\n 'none',\n 'Make failed GPU pipeline compilation reject cleanly, and remove resource disposal listeners when a renderer is disposed.'\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n 'The source-inspired vertical slice, controller-first UX and explicit attract-mode, procedural-audio and testing requirements give the game a clear identity.',\n 'No internet research is allowed while a live integration URL must be followed; I treated reading the supplied protocol files as integration work.',\n 'Combining a polished three-sector campaign, procedural audiovisuals, multiple input styles and real multiplayer in one self-contained HTML file.',\n 'Separate required protocol documentation from the no-research rule, and clarify whether standalone multiplayer requires relay hosting for restrictive networks.'\n]\nopen(p,'w').write(json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np='main.js';s=open(p).read();needle='const d = document.createElement(\\\"div\\\");\\\\n\\\\tfor (const [key, val] of Object.entries(META.sourceInformation))'\nif needle in s:\n s=s.replace(needle,'const sourceHeading=document.createElement(\\\"h3\\\");sourceHeading.textContent=\\\"Source Information\\\";root.append(sourceHeading);\\\\n\\\\tconst d = document.createElement(\\\"div\\\");\\\\n\\\\tfor (const [key, val] of Object.entries(META.sourceInformation))')\nelse:\n print('Source heading insertion pattern not found')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='transport_tests.py';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"__game.set('lives',1);__game.set('health',1);__game.tick(2);__game.hurt(1)\\\",\\\"__game.tick(3);__game.set('lives',1);__game.set('health',1);__game.hurt(1)\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nbiome check --write --linter-enabled=false --assist-enabled=false main.js\nruff format transport_tests.py\nruff check test.py transport_tests.py hub-tests.py preview.py\nnpm test --silent\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
